See: https://github.com/hanjq17/Spectrum

The Chebyshev forecaster is adapted from that repository (MIT). The dgenerate
integration keeps the forecaster state on the pipeline for one call and restores
the original block forwards when the call ends.

Spectrum forecasts the denoiser's block outputs with a Chebyshev fit blended
with a one-step Taylor step, then skips those blocks on later diffusion steps.
Embeddings and the final projection still run, so the forecast is placed in the
current timestep's output head. On SDXL the cached tensor is the last up
block, and the output convolution still runs.
